From: "Pluet, LLC" <358065800+pluetllc@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ao_audiounit: ask the route for the stream's sample rate

The output opened the session at whatever rate the route had and let the
RemoteIO unit convert, so 96 kHz and 192 kHz TrueHD or DTS-HD MA decoded to
PCM were resampled to the route's rate inside the unit without a word. It
now asks the session for the stream's own rate (public
setPreferredSampleRate) before activating it, logs what the route gives
(rate and channels), and when the route keeps a different rate, opens at
that rate so mpv's own resampler converts once, visibly in audio-out-params,
instead of the unit doing it hidden. Format and channel order are as
before: mpv's samples, 24-bit decodes exact in float, channels by the unit's
labels, unity gain at 100% volume.

---
diff --git a/audio/out/ao_audiounit.m b/audio/out/ao_audiounit.m
index 33292b3..eb344fc 100644
--- a/audio/out/ao_audiounit.m
+++ b/audio/out/ao_audiounit.m
@@ -17,6 +17,8 @@
 
 #include "ao.h"
 #include "internal.h"
+#include <math.h>
+
 #include "audio/format.h"
 #include "osdep/timer.h"
 #include "options/m_option.h"
@@ -127,8 +129,17 @@ static bool init_audiounit(struct ao *ao)
 
     [instance setCategory:AVAudioSessionCategoryPlayback withOptions:options error:nil];
     [instance setMode:AVAudioSessionModeMoviePlayback error:nil];
+    // Ask for the stream's own rate (96 or 192 kHz TrueHD and DTS-HD MA),
+    // so nothing is resampled where the route takes it; the system decides.
+    [instance setPreferredSampleRate:ao->samplerate error:nil];
     [instance setActive:YES error:nil];
     [instance setPreferredOutputNumberOfChannels:prefChannels error:nil];
+    MP_INFO(ao, "route: %d Hz asked, %.0f Hz out; %ld of %ld channels\n", ao->samplerate,
+            instance.sampleRate, (long)instance.outputNumberOfChannels, (long)maxChannels);
+    // A rate the route keeps different is converted once, here by mpv's
+    // resampler, instead of inside the output unit.
+    if (instance.sampleRate >= 8000 && lrint(instance.sampleRate) != ao->samplerate)
+        ao->samplerate = (int)lrint(instance.sampleRate);
 
     AudioComponentDescription desc = (AudioComponentDescription) {
         .componentType         = kAudioUnitType_Output,
